{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1407","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Discrete Centrifugal Jumps"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ beautiful skyscrapers in New York, the height of the $$$i$$$-th one is $$$h_i$$$. Today some villains have set on fire first $$$n - 1$$$ of them, and now the only safety building is $$$n$$$-th skyscraper."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a jump from $$$i$$$-th skyscraper to $$$j$$$-th ($$$i \\lt j$$$) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"discrete"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if all skyscrapers between are strictly lower or higher than both of them. Formally, jump is discrete, if $$$i \\lt j$$$ and one of the following conditions satisfied: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$i + 1 = j$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\max(h_{i + 1}, \\ldots, h_{j - 1}) \\lt \\min(h_i, h_j)$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\max(h_i, h_j) \\lt \\min(h_{i + 1}, \\ldots, h_{j - 1})$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At the moment, Vasya is staying on the first skyscraper and wants to live a little longer, so his goal is to reach $$$n$$$-th skyscraper with minimal count of discrete jumps. Help him with calcualting this number."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 3 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — total amount of skyscrapers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$h_1, h_2, \\ldots, h_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le h_i \\le 10^9$$$) — heights of skyscrapers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print single number $$$k$$$ — minimal amount of discrete jumps. We can show that an answer always exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n1 3 1 4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n4 2 2 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n100 1 100 1 100\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first testcase, Vasya can jump in the following way: $$$1 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 4 \\rightarrow 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second and third testcases, we can reach last skyscraper in one jump."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sequence of jumps in the fourth testcase: $$$1 \\rightarrow 3 \\rightarrow 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1407D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1407/problem/D"}